# Cross-session memory scenarios (Path B headline metric — docs/path-b-memory.md §7).
# Each line establishes fact(s) in earlier session(s) ("setup"), then a later-session
# "question" that depends on them. A correct answer contains every "expected" substring.
# Facts are project-specific / invented so a no-memory ("cold") run cannot guess them.
# The guard suite's cross-session set (owiki eval --guards, Path C M.2). comment-language accepts "Englisch":
# the scenario asks for answers in German, and the remembered preference is followed.
{"name": "chat-model", "setup": "User: For all our OpenWiki work, let's standardize on qwen3:30b as the default chat model.\nAssistant: Understood — qwen3:30b is our default chat model from now on.", "question": "Which chat model did we standardize on as the default?", "expected": ["qwen3:30b"]}
{"name": "graph-db", "setup": "User: We picked Kuzu as our graph database, because it stores the whole graph in a single file.\nAssistant: Noted — Kuzu is our graph database, chosen for its single-file store.", "question": "What graph database did we choose, and what was the reason?", "expected": ["Kuzu", "single"]}
{"name": "serve-port", "setup": "User: For this project, always run the web UI on port 8137.\nAssistant: Got it — I'll serve the OpenWiki web UI on port 8137.", "question": "Which port should I run the OpenWiki web UI on?", "expected": ["8137"]}
{"name": "embedding-model", "setup": "User: The embedding model for this project is bge-m3, since the corpus is German and bge-m3 is multilingual.\nAssistant: Understood — bge-m3 for embeddings, chosen for its multilingual / German support.", "question": "Which embedding model are we using for this project?", "expected": ["bge-m3"]}
{"name": "release-date", "setup": ["User: Quick note — the OpenWiki v1.0 release is scheduled for March 15th.\nAssistant: Noted — v1.0 is targeted for March 15th.", "User: Separately, let's plan to add a Docling source parser and improve the graph tab's label declutter later.\nAssistant: Sure — a Docling parser can slot in behind sources.parse_source, and the declutter heuristic could use real text widths.\nUser: Good, and maybe a dark mode for the SPA too.\nAssistant: Agreed, a dark mode would be a nice touch."], "question": "When is the OpenWiki v1.0 release scheduled?", "expected": ["March 15"]}
{"name": "comment-language", "setup": "User: I'd like answers in German for this project.\nAssistant: Verstanden — ich antworte auf Deutsch.\nUser: But keep the code comments in English.\nAssistant: Alles klar — Kommentare auf Englisch, Antworten auf Deutsch.", "question": "What language should the code comments be written in for this project?", "expected": ["English|Englisch"]}
{"name": "license", "setup": "User: We decided OpenWiki will be released under the MIT license.\nAssistant: Noted — MIT license for OpenWiki.", "question": "Under which license will OpenWiki be released?", "expected": ["MIT"]}
{"name": "changed-branch", "setup": ["User: Our default git branch for this project is master.\nAssistant: Noted — the default branch is master.", "User: We renamed the default git branch from master to main.\nAssistant: Understood — the default git branch is now main."], "question": "What is the current default git branch for this project?", "expected": ["main"]}
